      "body": "The full-scan paged MQA logits get the indexer head weights in fp32, so DeepGEMM runs its fp32 reduce; the sparse-set and prefill-table scorers in the same file already pass them as bf16. Cast them to bf16 at the two full-scan calls as well.\n\nDecode step on GB300 at fixed batch: numbers to follow.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40043591577](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40043591577)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40043591288](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40043591288)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40043591341](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40043591341)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
      "changedFiles": 1,
      "comments": {
        "nodes": [
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "kpham-sgl"
            },
            "body": "Closing: this is a no-op. `deep_gemm_fp4_paged_mqa_logits` already casts the head weights with `weights.to(index_weights_dtype())` and requests `index_logits_dtype()` logits, which since #45880 resolve to bf16 on SM100 (GB300 included), so the full-scan calls already run DeepGEMM's bf16 path. A fixed-batch A/B on GB300 (DP attention 4, EP 4) measured 0.02 to 0.4% between the arms, within noise.",
